IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgk-part9-declared`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 9 (Investigations), ss 232 to 236: inspectors appointed at the direction of the Minister on application, their reports, a related corporation,
-- and the procedure and powers of an inspector (s 234 is repealed). The party and act types of the regulative rules are in sgk-part9-declared.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The Minister, the inspectors and the Court appear only as what their acts mean to the person.
-- Marks in the comments: "FALSE-kind" and "NOTHING-kind" say why a branch answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING; "fork F-Kn" points at the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `Section 232: an investigation on application`

-- src:22038 | (a) in the case of a company having a share capital, on the
-- src:22039 | application of —
-- src:22041 | (i) not less than 200 members (excluding the company
-- src:22042 | itself if it is registered as a member) or of members
-- src:22043 | holding not less than 10% of the shares issued
-- src:22044 | (excluding treasury shares); or
@ref s 232(1)(a)(i) (src:22038-22044)
GIVEN `the number of members who apply, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares held by the members who apply` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares issued, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(1)(a)(i) the application is made by enough members` MEANS
        `the number of members who apply, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` AT LEAST 200      -- "not less than 200 members"
     OR (`the number of shares issued, excluding treasury shares` GREATER THAN 0
         AND 10 TIMES `the number of shares held by the members who apply` AT LEAST `the number of shares issued, excluding treasury shares`)   -- "members holding not less than 10% of the shares issued (excluding treasury shares)"

-- src:22046 | (ii) holders of debentures holding not less than 20% in
-- src:22047 | nominal value of debentures issued;
@ref s 232(1)(a)(ii) (src:22046-22047)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the debentures held by the holders who apply, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the debentures issued, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(1)(a)(ii) the application is made by enough debenture holders` MEANS
        `the nominal value of the debentures issued, in Singapore dollars` GREATER THAN 0
    AND 5 TIMES `the nominal value of the debentures held by the holders who apply, in Singapore dollars` AT LEAST `the nominal value of the debentures issued, in Singapore dollars`   -- "not less than 20% in nominal value of debentures issued"

-- src:22049 | (b) in the case of a company not having a share capital, on the
-- src:22050 | application of not less than 20% in number of the persons
-- src:22051 | on the company’s register of members; or
@ref s 232(1)(b) (src:22049-22051)
GIVEN `the number of persons who apply, among the persons on the company's register of members` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of persons on the company's register of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 232(1)(b) the application is made by enough of the persons on the register of members` MEANS
        `the number of persons on the company's register of members` GREATER THAN 0
    AND 5 TIMES `the number of persons who apply, among the persons on the company's register of members` AT LEAST `the number of persons on the company's register of members`   -- "not less than 20% in number of the persons on the company's register of members"

-- src:22033 | 232.—(1) The Minister may appoint one or more inspectors to
-- src:22034 | investigate the affairs of a company or such aspects of the affairs of a
-- src:22035 | company as are specified in the instrument of appointment and to
-- src:22036 | report thereon in such manner as the Minister directs —
-- src:22038 | (a) in the case of a company having a share capital, on the
-- src:22039 | application of —
-- src:22041 | (i) not less than 200 members (excluding the company
-- src:22042 | itself if it is registered as a member) or of members
-- src:22043 | holding not less than 10% of the shares issued
-- src:22044 | (excluding treasury shares); or
-- src:22046 | (ii) holders of debentures holding not less than 20% in
-- src:22047 | nominal value of debentures issued;
-- src:22049 | (b) in the case of a company not having a share capital, on the
-- src:22050 | application of not less than 20% in number of the persons
-- src:22051 | on the company’s register of members; or
-- src:22053 | (c) in any case on the application of a company pursuant to a
-- src:22054 | special resolution.
@ref s 232(1) (src:22033-22054)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members who apply, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares held by the members who apply` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares issued, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the debentures held by the holders who apply, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the debentures issued, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of persons who apply, among the persons on the company's register of members` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of persons on the company's register of members` IS A NUMBER
      `the company applies pursuant to a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(1) the Minister may appoint inspectors on the application` MEANS
    IF    (`the company has a share capital`
           AND (   `s 232(1)(a)(i) the application is made by enough members` `the number of members who apply, excluding the company itself if it is registered as a member` `the number of shares held by the members who apply` `the number of shares issued, excluding treasury shares`
                OR `s 232(1)(a)(ii) the application is made by enough debenture holders` `the nominal value of the debentures held by the holders who apply, in Singapore dollars` `the nominal value of the debentures issued, in Singapore dollars`))
       OR ((NOT `the company has a share capital`)
           AND `s 232(1)(b) the application is made by enough of the persons on the register of members` `the number of persons who apply, among the persons on the company's register of members` `the number of persons on the company's register of members`)
       OR `the company applies pursuant to a special resolution`     -- (c) "in any case"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister "may appoint ... on the application of" the applicants the paragraphs name; the section does not say that the Minister may not act on any other application (split site (ii): "on application", not "where", "when" or "upon"; fork F-K24)

-- src:22059 | (2) An application under this section must be supported by such
-- src:22060 | evidence as the Minister requires as to the reasons for the application
-- src:22061 | and the motives of the applicants in requiring the investigation, and
-- src:22062 | the Minister may before appointing an inspector require the
-- src:22063 | applicants to give security for such amount as the Minister thinks
-- src:22064 | fit for payment of the cost of the investigation.
@ref s 232(2) (src:22059-22064)
GIVEN `the Minister requires evidence as to the reasons for the application and the motives of the applicants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(2) the application must be supported by the evidence the Minister requires` MEANS
    IF `the Minister requires evidence as to the reasons for the application and the motives of the applicants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty is to support the application with "such evidence as the Minister requires"; where none is required it asks for none (fork F-K5)

@ref s 232(2) (src:22059-22064)
GIVEN `the Minister has not yet appointed an inspector on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(2) the Minister may require the applicants to give security for the cost of the investigation` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has not yet appointed an inspector on the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the Minister "may before appointing an inspector require the applicants to give security"; a "may" gated by "before" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork F-K7)

§ `Section 233: the inspector's reports, and what the Minister may do with them`

-- src:22068 | 233.—(1) An inspector appointed by the Minister may, and if so
-- src:22069 | directed by the Minister must, make interim reports to the Minister
-- src:22070 | and on the conclusion of the investigation the inspector must report
-- src:22071 | the inspector’s opinion on or in relation to the affairs that the
-- src:22072 | inspector has been appointed to investigate together with the facts
-- src:22073 | upon which the inspector’s opinion is based to the Minister, and a
-- src:22074 | copy of the report must, subject to subsection (1B), be forwarded by
-- src:22075 | the Minister to the registered office of the company, and a further
-- src:22076 | copy must, subject to that subsection, at the request of the applicants
-- src:22077 | be delivered to them.
@ref s 233(1) (src:22068-22077)
GIVEN `the person is an inspector appointed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1) the inspector may make interim reports to the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the person is an inspector appointed by the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "An inspector appointed by the Minister"

@ref s 233(1) (src:22068-22077)
GIVEN `the Minister has directed the inspector to make an interim report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1) the inspector must make an interim report to the Minister` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has directed the inspector to make an interim report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an inspector "may, and if so directed by the Minister must, make interim reports"; an "if" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

@ref s 233(1) (src:22068-22077)
GIVEN `the investigation has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion under subsection (1B) that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1) the Minister must forward a copy of the report to the registered office of the company` MEANS
    IF `the Minister is of the opinion under subsection (1B) that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or any part of it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the forwarding is "subject to subsection (1B)", and under (1B) "The Minister is not bound to furnish a company ... with a copy of the report or any part thereof if the Minister is of the opinion that there is good reason for not divulging"
    ELSE (IF `the investigation has concluded`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the copy is forwarded when "on the conclusion of the investigation the inspector must report" and the report has been made; not before (fork F-K5)

@ref s 233(1) (src:22068-22077)
GIVEN `the investigation has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicants have requested a further copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion under subsection (1B) that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1) the Minister must deliver a further copy of the report to the applicants` MEANS
    IF `the Minister is of the opinion under subsection (1B) that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or any part of it`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a further copy must, subject to that subsection, at the request of the applicants be delivered to them"; under (1B) the Minister "is not bound to furnish ... an applicant ... with a copy of the report or any part thereof"
    ELSE (IF `the investigation has concluded` AND `the applicants have requested a further copy`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the further copy is delivered "at the request of the applicants" once the report is made; an "at the request" ("upon") unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

-- src:22079 | (1A) Subject to subsections (1B) and (1C), the Minister must give a
-- src:22080 | copy of a report made under this Part to each person to whom in the
-- src:22081 | opinion of the Minister the report ought to be given by reason that it
-- src:22082 | relates to the affairs of that person to a material extent.
-- src:22084 | (1B) The Minister is not bound to furnish a company, an applicant
-- src:22085 | or any other person with a copy of the report or any part thereof if the
-- src:22086 | Minister is of the opinion that there is good reason for not divulging
-- src:22087 | the contents of the report or any part thereof.
-- src:22089 | (1C) Subject to subsection (1D), the Minister must not give a copy
-- src:22090 | of a report made under this Part to a person under subsection (1A) if
-- src:22091 | the Minister believes that legal proceedings that have been or, in the
-- src:22092 | Minister’s opinion, might be instituted, might be unduly prejudiced
-- src:22093 | by giving the report to that person.
-- src:22095 | (1D) A court before which legal proceedings are brought against a
-- src:22096 | person for or in respect of matters dealt with in a report under this Part
-- src:22097 | may order that a copy of the report or part thereof must be given to
-- src:22098 | that person.
@ref s 233(1A) to (1D) (src:22079-22098)
GIVEN `in the Minister's opinion the report ought to be given to the person by reason that it relates to the person's affairs to a material extent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is of the opinion under subsection (1B) that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or any part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister believes that legal proceedings that have been or might be instituted might be unduly prejudiced by giving the report to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court before which legal proceedings are brought against the person for or in respect of matters dealt with in the report has ordered that a copy be given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1A) the Minister must give the person a copy of the report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a court before which legal proceedings are brought against the person for or in respect of matters dealt with in the report has ordered that a copy be given to the person`
        THEN JUST TRUE    -- (1D): the court "may order that a copy of the report or part thereof must be given to that person"; (1C) is "Subject to subsection (1D)" (fork F-K20: the order is taken to prevail over (1B) too)
        IF `the Minister believes that legal proceedings that have been or might be instituted might be unduly prejudiced by giving the report to the person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Minister must not give a copy of a report ... to a person under subsection (1A) if the Minister believes that legal proceedings ... might be unduly prejudiced" (s 233(1C))
        IF `the Minister is of the opinion under subsection (1B) that there is good reason for not divulging the contents of the report or any part of it`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): (1A) is "Subject to subsections (1B) and (1C)", and "The Minister is not bound to furnish a company, an applicant or any other person with a copy of the report or any part thereof if the Minister is of the opinion that there is good reason for not divulging" (s 233(1B))
        IF `in the Minister's opinion the report ought to be given to the person by reason that it relates to the person's affairs to a material extent`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty is to give a copy "to each person to whom in the opinion of the Minister the report ought to be given by reason that it relates to the affairs of that person to a material extent"; a "where"-type gate unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

@ref s 233(1C) (src:22089-22098)
GIVEN `the Minister believes that legal proceedings that have been or might be instituted might be unduly prejudiced by giving the report to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court before which legal proceedings are brought against the person for or in respect of matters dealt with in the report has ordered that a copy be given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1C) the Minister must not give the person a copy of the report under subsection (1A)` MEANS
    IF `the Minister believes that legal proceedings that have been or might be instituted might be unduly prejudiced by giving the report to the person` AND (NOT `a court before which legal proceedings are brought against the person for or in respect of matters dealt with in the report has ordered that a copy be given to the person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar applies "if the Minister believes" and is "Subject to subsection (1D)"; a bar's own question, with its "if" unmet or its "subject to" met (fork F-K25)

-- src:22095 | (1D) A court before which legal proceedings are brought against a
-- src:22096 | person for or in respect of matters dealt with in a report under this Part
-- src:22097 | may order that a copy of the report or part thereof must be given to
-- src:22098 | that person.
@ref s 233(1D) (src:22095-22098)
GIVEN `legal proceedings are brought against the person for or in respect of matters dealt with in the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the court before which the proceedings are brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(1D) the court may order that a copy of the report or part of it be given to the person` MEANS
    IF `legal proceedings are brought against the person for or in respect of matters dealt with in the report` AND `the person is the court before which the proceedings are brought`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is stated for "A court before which legal proceedings are brought against a person for or in respect of matters dealt with in a report"; the subsection says nothing of any other court

-- The Minister's duties and prohibition as regulative rules. (1) and (1A) have no time limit and no stated consequence, so no trace can show them breached;
-- (1C) is a prohibition, so the act is the breach.
-- src:22068 | 233.—(1) An inspector appointed by the Minister may, and if so
-- src:22069 | directed by the Minister must, make interim reports to the Minister
-- src:22070 | and on the conclusion of the investigation the inspector must report
-- src:22071 | the inspector’s opinion on or in relation to the affairs that the
-- src:22072 | inspector has been appointed to investigate together with the facts
-- src:22073 | upon which the inspector’s opinion is based to the Minister, and a
-- src:22074 | copy of the report must, subject to subsection (1B), be forwarded by
-- src:22075 | the Minister to the registered office of the company, and a further
-- src:22076 | copy must, subject to that subsection, at the request of the applicants
-- src:22077 | be delivered to them.
@ref s 233(1) (src:22068-22077)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 233(1) the inspector must report to the Minister on the conclusion of the investigation` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 an inspector appointed under Part 9`
    MUST `s 233(1) report to the Minister the inspector's opinion on the affairs investigated, with the facts on which it is based`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 233(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 an inspector appointed under Part 9` BECAUSE "the inspector did not report to the Minister on the conclusion of the investigation" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 233(1) (src:22068-22077)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 233(1) the Minister must forward a copy of the report to the registered office` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister`
    MUST `s 233(1) forward a copy of the report to the registered office of the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 233(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not forward a copy of the report to the registered office of the company" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:22079 | (1A) Subject to subsections (1B) and (1C), the Minister must give a
-- src:22080 | copy of a report made under this Part to each person to whom in the
-- src:22081 | opinion of the Minister the report ought to be given by reason that it
-- src:22082 | relates to the affairs of that person to a material extent.
@ref s 233(1A) (src:22079-22082)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 233(1A) the Minister must give a copy of the report to the person whose affairs it relates to` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister`
    MUST `s 233(1A) give a copy of the report to a person whose affairs it relates to in a material extent`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 233(1A) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not give a copy of the report to a person whose affairs it relates to to a material extent" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:22089 | (1C) Subject to subsection (1D), the Minister must not give a copy
-- src:22090 | of a report made under this Part to a person under subsection (1A) if
-- src:22091 | the Minister believes that legal proceedings that have been or, in the
-- src:22092 | Minister’s opinion, might be instituted, might be unduly prejudiced
-- src:22093 | by giving the report to that person.
@ref s 233(1C) (src:22089-22093)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 233(1C) the Minister must not give a copy of the report where legal proceedings might be unduly prejudiced` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister`
    SHANT `s 233(1C) give a copy of the report to a person when legal proceedings might be unduly prejudiced`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister gave a copy of the report under subsection (1A) although legal proceedings might be unduly prejudiced"

-- src:22103 | (2) The Minister may, if he or she is of the opinion that it is
-- src:22104 | necessary in the public interest to do so, cause the report to be printed
-- src:22105 | and published but must refrain from so doing if the Attorney‑General
-- src:22106 | has certified in writing that publication of the report would be
-- src:22107 | prejudicial to the administration of justice.
@ref s 233(2) (src:22103-22107)
GIVEN `the Minister is of the opinion that it is necessary in the public interest to cause the report to be printed and published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General has certified in writing that publication of the report would be prejudicial to the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(2) the Minister may cause the report to be printed and published` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney-General has certified in writing that publication of the report would be prejudicial to the administration of justice`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the Minister "must refrain from so doing if the Attorney-General has certified in writing that publication of the report would be prejudicial to the administration of justice"
    ELSE (IF `the Minister is of the opinion that it is necessary in the public interest to cause the report to be printed and published`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister "may, if he or she is of the opinion that it is necessary in the public interest"; a "may" with an "if" (not "only if") gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K18)

@ref s 233(2) (src:22103-22107)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 233(2) the Minister must refrain from publishing the report when the Attorney-General has certified that publication would be prejudicial` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister`
    SHANT `s 233(2) publish the report when the Attorney-General has certified that publication would be prejudicial to the administration of justice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 231 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister published a report that the Attorney-General had certified in writing would be prejudicial to the administration of justice if published"

-- src:22109 | (3) If from any report of an inspector appointed by the Minister it
-- src:22110 | appears to the Minister that the case is one in which a prosecution
-- src:22111 | ought to be instituted, the Minister must cause a prosecution to be
-- src:22112 | instituted accordingly and all officers and agents of the company
-- src:22113 | (other than the defendant in the proceedings) must on being required
-- src:22114 | by the Minister to do so give all assistance in connection with the
-- src:22115 | prosecution which they are reasonably able to give.
@ref s 233(3) (src:22109-22115)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister from the report of an inspector that the case is one in which a prosecution ought to be instituted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(3) the Minister must cause a prosecution to be instituted` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Minister from the report of an inspector that the case is one in which a prosecution ought to be instituted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "If from any report of an inspector appointed by the Minister it appears to the Minister that the case is one in which a prosecution ought to be instituted"; an "if" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

@ref s 233(3) (src:22109-22115)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the defendant in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has required the person to give assistance in connection with the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is assistance which the person is reasonably able to give` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(3) the officer or agent must give the Minister all assistance in connection with the prosecution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is an officer or agent of the company`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for "all officers and agents of the company"; it says nothing of anyone else (a scope limit with no "only": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
        IF `the person is the defendant in the proceedings`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all officers and agents of the company (other than the defendant in the proceedings)"
        IF NOT `the Minister has required the person to give assistance in connection with the prosecution`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "on being required by the Minister to do so"; an "on" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)
        IF NOT `the assistance is assistance which the person is reasonably able to give`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all assistance in connection with the prosecution which they are reasonably able to give"; a duty limited by its own wording (fork F-K26)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 233(3) (src:22109-22115)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 233(3) the Minister must cause a prosecution to be instituted` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister`
    MUST `s 233(3) institute a prosecution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 233(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 the Minister` BECAUSE "the Minister did not cause a prosecution to be instituted although it appeared from the report of an inspector that one ought to be" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 233(3) (src:22109-22115)
GIVEN `the name of the officer or agent` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 233(3) the officer or agent must give the assistance on being required by the Minister` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 an officer or agent of a corporation` `the name of the officer or agent`
    MUST `s 233(3) give the Minister all assistance in connection with the prosecution that the person is reasonably able to give`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 233(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 an officer or agent of a corporation` `the name of the officer or agent` BECAUSE "the officer or agent did not give the assistance required by the Minister in connection with the prosecution" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:22117 | (4) If from any report of an inspector appointed by the Minister it
-- src:22118 | appears to the Minister that proceedings ought in the public interest to
-- src:22119 | be brought by any company dealt with by the report for the recovery
-- src:22120 | of damages in respect of any fraud, misfeasance or other misconduct
-- src:22121 | in connection with the promotion or formation of that company or in
-- src:22122 | the management of its affairs or for the recovery of any property of
-- src:22123 | the company which has been misapplied or wrongfully retained, the
-- src:22124 | Minister may himself or herself bring proceedings for that purpose in
-- src:22125 | the name of the company.
@ref s 233(4) (src:22117-22125)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister from the report of an inspector that proceedings ought in the public interest to be brought by the company for the recovery of damages in respect of fraud, misfeasance or other misconduct in connection with its promotion or formation or in the management of its affairs, or for the recovery of any property of the company which has been misapplied or wrongfully retained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233(4) the Minister may bring proceedings in the name of the company` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Minister from the report of an inspector that proceedings ought in the public interest to be brought by the company for the recovery of damages in respect of fraud, misfeasance or other misconduct in connection with its promotion or formation or in the management of its affairs, or for the recovery of any property of the company which has been misapplied or wrongfully retained`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister "may himself or herself bring proceedings" if the report shows proceedings ought in the public interest to be brought; a "may" with an "if" (not "only if") gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K18)

§ `Section 235: a related corporation`

-- src:22131 | 235. Where an inspector thinks it necessary for the purposes of the
-- src:22132 | investigation of the affairs of a company to investigate the affairs of a
-- src:22133 | corporation which is or has at any relevant time been a corporation
-- src:22134 | deemed to be related by virtue of section 6 to the company, the
-- src:22135 | inspector may, with the consent in writing of the Minister, investigate
-- src:22136 | the affairs of that corporation.
@ref s 235 (src:22131-22136)
GIVEN `the inspector thinks it necessary for the purposes of the investigation of the affairs of the company to investigate the affairs of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other corporation is or has at any relevant time been a corporation deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235 the inspector may investigate the affairs of the other corporation` MEANS
    IF    `the inspector thinks it necessary for the purposes of the investigation of the affairs of the company to investigate the affairs of the other corporation`
       AND `the other corporation is or has at any relevant time been a corporation deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6`
       AND `the Minister has consented in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the inspector "may, with the consent in writing of the Minister, investigate the affairs of that corporation" where the inspector thinks it necessary; the section does not say the inspector may not otherwise (split site (ii): "with the consent of"; fork F-K21; section 236(1) gives the inspector the power without mentioning consent: fork F-K22)

§ `Section 236: procedure and powers of an inspector`

-- src:22140 | 236.—(1) If an inspector appointed to investigate the affairs of a
-- src:22141 | company thinks it necessary for the purposes of the investigation to
-- src:22142 | investigate also the affairs of any other corporation which is or has at
-- src:22143 | any relevant time been deemed to be or to have been related to that
-- src:22148 | company by virtue of section 6, the inspector has power to do so, and
-- src:22149 | the inspector must report on the affairs of the other corporation so far
-- src:22150 | as the inspector thinks the results of the investigation thereof are
-- src:22151 | relevant to the investigation of the affairs of the company.
@ref s 236(1) (src:22140-22151)
GIVEN `the inspector appointed to investigate the affairs of a company thinks it necessary for the purposes of the investigation to investigate also the affairs of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other corporation is or has at any relevant time been a corporation deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(1) the inspector has power to investigate also the affairs of the other corporation` MEANS
    IF `the inspector appointed to investigate the affairs of a company thinks it necessary for the purposes of the investigation to investigate also the affairs of the other corporation` AND `the other corporation is or has at any relevant time been a corporation deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an inspector ... thinks it necessary ... to investigate also the affairs of any other corporation which is or has at any relevant time been deemed ... related ..., the inspector has power to do so": a power-named function with an "if" (not "only if") gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K18; and F-K22 against section 235)

@ref s 236(1) (src:22140-22151)
GIVEN `the inspector has investigated the affairs of the other corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(1) the inspector must report on the affairs of the other corporation so far as the inspector thinks the results of the investigation relevant` MEANS
    IF `the inspector has investigated the affairs of the other corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty to report follows the investigation of the other corporation ("the inspector has power to do so, and the inspector must report on the affairs of the other corporation"); with none made there is nothing to report on (fork F-K5)

@ref s 236(1) (src:22140-22151)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 236(1) the inspector must report on the affairs of the related corporation` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 an inspector appointed under Part 9`
    MUST `s 236(1) report on the affairs of the related corporation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 236(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 an inspector appointed under Part 9` BECAUSE "the inspector did not report on the affairs of the other corporation investigated" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (2): two duties in one sentence: "must, if required by an inspector ..., produce ... and must give ... all assistance ... reasonably able to give". Read as two duties; only the first depends on the requirement (fork F-K23).
-- src:22153 | (2) Every officer and agent of a corporation the affairs of which are
-- src:22154 | being investigated under this Part must, if required by an inspector
-- src:22155 | appointed under this Part, produce to the inspector all books and
-- src:22156 | documents in the officer’s or agent’s custody or power and must give
-- src:22157 | to the inspector all assistance in connection with the investigation
-- src:22158 | which he or she is reasonably able to give.
@ref s 236(2) (src:22153-22158)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an inspector has required the person to produce the books and documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(2) the officer or agent must produce to the inspector all books and documents in the officer's or agent's custody or power` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for "Every officer and agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under this Part"; the subsection says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE (IF `an inspector has required the person to produce the books and documents`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty to produce arises "if required by an inspector"; an "if" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

@ref s 236(2) (src:22153-22158)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is assistance in connection with the investigation which the person is reasonably able to give` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(2) the officer or agent must give the inspector all assistance in connection with the investigation` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for "Every officer and agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under this Part"
    ELSE (IF `the assistance is assistance in connection with the investigation which the person is reasonably able to give`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all assistance in connection with the investigation which he or she is reasonably able to give"; a duty limited by its own wording (fork F-K26)

@ref s 236(2) (src:22153-22158)
GIVEN `the name of the officer or agent` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 236(2) the officer or agent must produce the books and documents and give the assistance` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 an officer or agent of a corporation` `the name of the officer or agent`
    MUST `s 236(2) produce to the inspector all books and documents in the person's custody or power and give all assistance reasonably able`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 236(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 an officer or agent of a corporation` `the name of the officer or agent` BECAUSE "the officer or agent did not produce the books and documents or give the assistance an inspector required" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:22160 | (3) An inspector may, by notice in the prescribed form, require any
-- src:22161 | officer or agent of any corporation whose affairs are being
-- src:22162 | investigated pursuant to this Part to appear for examination on oath
-- src:22163 | or affirmation (which the inspector is hereby authorised to
-- src:22164 | administer) in relation to its business; and the notice may require
-- src:22165 | the production of all books and documents in the custody or under the
-- src:22166 | control of that officer or agent.
@ref s 236(3) (src:22160-22166)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is made by notice in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(3) the inspector may require the person to appear for examination on oath or affirmation` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` AND `the requirement is made by notice in the prescribed form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is stated "by notice in the prescribed form" and for "any officer or agent of any corporation whose affairs are being investigated pursuant to this Part"; the subsection says nothing of any other requirement

-- src:22168 | (4) An inspector who, pursuant to this section, requires the
-- src:22169 | production of all books and documents in the custody or power or
-- src:22170 | under the control of an officer or agent of any corporation whose
-- src:22171 | affairs are being investigated under or pursuant to this Part —
-- src:22173 | (a) may take possession of all such books and documents;
-- src:22175 | (b) may retain all such books and documents for such time as
-- src:22176 | the inspector considers to be necessary for the purpose of
-- src:22177 | the investigation; and
-- src:22179 | (c) must permit such corporation to have access at all
-- src:22180 | reasonable times to all such books and documents so
-- src:22181 | long as they are in his or her possession.
@ref s 236(4) (src:22168-22181)
GIVEN `the inspector has required the production of all books and documents in the custody or power or under the control of an officer or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(4)(a) the inspector may take possession of all the books and documents` MEANS
    IF `the inspector has required the production of all books and documents in the custody or power or under the control of an officer or agent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) speaks of "An inspector who, pursuant to this section, requires the production of all books and documents"

@ref s 236(4) (src:22168-22181)
GIVEN `the inspector has required the production of all books and documents in the custody or power or under the control of an officer or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is one the inspector considers necessary for the purpose of the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(4)(b) the inspector may retain the books and documents for the time` MEANS
    IF `the inspector has required the production of all books and documents in the custody or power or under the control of an officer or agent` AND `the time is one the inspector considers necessary for the purpose of the investigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the inspector may retain "for such time as the inspector considers to be necessary for the purpose of the investigation"; a longer time is outside the limit and the paragraph says nothing of it

@ref s 236(4) (src:22168-22181)
GIVEN `the inspector has required the production of all books and documents in the custody or power or under the control of an officer or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the books and documents are in the inspector's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(4)(c) the inspector must permit the corporation to have access to the books and documents` MEANS
    IF NOT `the inspector has required the production of all books and documents in the custody or power or under the control of an officer or agent`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) speaks of "An inspector who, pursuant to this section, requires the production of all books and documents"
    ELSE (IF `the books and documents are in the inspector's possession` AND `the time is a reasonable time`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): access "at all reasonable times ... so long as they are in his or her possession"; the duty lapses outside reasonable times or when the inspector no longer has them ("so long as": periods ruling of 2026-11-05)

@ref s 236(4)(c) (src:22168-22181)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 236(4)(c) the inspector must permit the corporation to have access to the books and documents` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 an inspector appointed under Part 9`
    MUST `s 236(4)(c) permit the corporation to have access to the books and documents taken possession of`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 236(4)(c) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY `s 231 an inspector appointed under Part 9` BECAUSE "the inspector did not permit the corporation to have access at a reasonable time to the books and documents taken possession of" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:22183 | (4A) If an inspector has reasonable grounds for believing that a
-- src:22184 | director or past director of the company or of a corporation which is
-- src:22185 | or has at any time been deemed to be or to have been related to that
-- src:22186 | company by virtue of section 6 (called in this subsection the related
-- src:22187 | corporation) whose affairs the inspector is investigating maintains or
-- src:22188 | has maintained a bank account of any description, whether alone or
-- src:22189 | jointly with another person and whether in Singapore or elsewhere,
-- src:22194 | into or out of which there has been paid any money which has been in
-- src:22195 | any way connected with any act or omission or series of acts or
-- src:22196 | omissions, which on the part of that director or past director
-- src:22197 | constituted misconduct (whether fraudulent or not towards that
-- src:22198 | company or that related corporation or its members), an inspector
-- src:22199 | may require the director or past director to produce to the inspector all
-- src:22200 | documents in the director’s or past director’s possession or under his
-- src:22201 | or her control relating to that bank account.
-- src:22203 | [Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]
@ref s 236(4A) (src:22183-22203)
GIVEN `the person is a director or past director of the company or of a related corporation whose affairs the inspector is investigating` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspector has reasonable grounds for believing that the person maintains or has maintained a bank account of any description, whether alone or jointly with another person and whether in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspector has reasonable grounds for believing that money connected with an act or omission, or series of acts or omissions, that on the part of the person constituted misconduct has been paid into or out of the account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(4A) the inspector may require the person to produce all documents in the person's possession or under the person's control relating to the bank account` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director or past director of the company or of a related corporation whose affairs the inspector is investigating`
       AND `the inspector has reasonable grounds for believing that the person maintains or has maintained a bank account of any description, whether alone or jointly with another person and whether in Singapore or elsewhere`
       AND `the inspector has reasonable grounds for believing that money connected with an act or omission, or series of acts or omissions, that on the part of the person constituted misconduct has been paid into or out of the account`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an inspector has reasonable grounds for believing ... an inspector may require"; a "may" with an "if" (not "only if") gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K18). The subsection is dated by its tag "[Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]" (finding 6)

-- src:22205 | (5) If any officer or agent of any corporation, the affairs of which
-- src:22206 | are being investigated pursuant to this Part, fails to comply with the
-- src:22207 | requirements of any notice issued under subsection (3) or fails or
-- src:22208 | refuses to answer any question which is put to him or her by an
-- src:22209 | inspector with respect to the affairs of the corporation or that officer
-- src:22210 | or agent is a director or past director to whom subsection (4A)
-- src:22211 | applies, if he or she fails to comply with a requirement of an inspector
-- src:22212 | under that subsection, the inspector may certify the failure or refusal
-- src:22213 | under the hand of the inspector to the Court, which may thereupon
-- src:22214 | inquire into the case and, after hearing any witnesses against or on
-- src:22215 | behalf of the alleged offender and any statement offered in defence,
-- src:22216 | punish the offender in like manner as if the offender had been guilty
-- src:22217 | of contempt of the Court.
@ref s 236(5) (src:22205-22217)
GIVEN `the officer or agent has failed to comply with the requirements of a notice issued under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer or agent has failed or refused to answer a question put to the officer or agent by an inspector with respect to the affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or past director to whom subsection (4A) applies and has failed to comply with a requirement of an inspector under that subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(5) the inspector may certify the failure or refusal to the Court` MEANS
    IF    `the officer or agent has failed to comply with the requirements of a notice issued under subsection (3)`
       OR `the officer or agent has failed or refused to answer a question put to the officer or agent by an inspector with respect to the affairs of the corporation`
       OR `the person is a director or past director to whom subsection (4A) applies and has failed to comply with a requirement of an inspector under that subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any officer or agent ... fails to comply ... or fails or refuses to answer ..., the inspector may certify the failure or refusal"; a "may" with an "if" (not "only if") gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K18)

@ref s 236(5) (src:22205-22217)
GIVEN `the inspector has certified the failure or refusal under the hand of the inspector to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has inquired into the case and heard any witnesses against or on behalf of the alleged offender and any statement offered in defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(5) the Court may punish the offender in like manner as if the offender had been guilty of contempt of the Court` MEANS
    IF `the inspector has certified the failure or refusal under the hand of the inspector to the Court` AND `the Court has inquired into the case and heard any witnesses against or on behalf of the alleged offender and any statement offered in defence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the Court "may thereupon inquire into the case and, after hearing any witnesses ... punish the offender"; a "may" gated by "thereupon" and "after hearing" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork F-K7)

-- src:22219 | (6) No person, who is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a
-- src:22220 | corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under this Part,
-- src:22221 | is entitled to refuse to answer any question which is relevant or
-- src:22222 | material to the investigation on the ground that the person’s answer
-- src:22223 | might tend to incriminate him or her but if the person claims that the
-- src:22224 | answer to any question, might incriminate him or her and but for this
-- src:22225 | subsection the person would have been entitled to refuse to answer
-- src:22226 | the question, the answer to the question may not be used in any
-- src:22227 | subsequent criminal proceedings except in the case of a charge
-- src:22228 | against the person for making a false statement in answer to that
-- src:22229 | question.
@ref s 236(6) (src:22219-22229)
GIVEN `the person is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is relevant or material to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(6) the person is entitled to refuse to answer the question on the ground that the answer might tend to incriminate the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` AND `the question is relevant or material to the investigation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person, who is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under this Part, is entitled to refuse to answer any question which is relevant or material to the investigation on the ground that the person's answer might tend to incriminate him or her"; an "entitled"-named function the Guide leaves open (fork F-K11)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (6) speaks of a person who is or was an officer or agent of the corporation investigated and of a question relevant or material to the investigation; subsection (7) governs anyone else

@ref s 236(6) (src:22219-22229)
GIVEN `the person is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is relevant or material to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claims that the answer might incriminate the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for subsection (6) the person would have been entitled to refuse to answer the question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a charge against the person for making a false statement in answer to the question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(6) the answer is barred from use in a subsequent criminal proceeding` MEANS
    IF    `the person is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9`
       AND `the question is relevant or material to the investigation`
       AND `the person claims that the answer might incriminate the person`
       AND `but for subsection (6) the person would have been entitled to refuse to answer the question`
    THEN (IF `the proceeding is a charge against the person for making a false statement in answer to the question`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the answer "may not be used in any subsequent criminal proceedings except in the case of a charge against the person for making a false statement in answer to that question"; an "except" met (fork F-K27)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- "the answer to the question may not be used in any subsequent criminal proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is stated for a person who claims that the answer might incriminate and who but for the subsection would have been entitled to refuse

-- src:22231 | (7) Subject to subsection (6), any person is entitled to refuse to
-- src:22232 | answer a question on the ground that the answer might tend to
-- src:22233 | incriminate him or her.
@ref s 236(7) (src:22231-22233)
GIVEN `the person is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is relevant or material to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer might tend to incriminate the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(7) the person is entitled to refuse to answer the question on the ground that the answer might tend to incriminate the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is or has formerly been an officer or agent of a corporation the affairs of which are being investigated under Part 9` AND `the question is relevant or material to the investigation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (6)": subsection (6) takes the entitlement away from such a person (an "entitled"-named function; fork F-K11)
    ELSE (IF `the answer might tend to incriminate the person`
          THEN JUST TRUE    -- "any person is entitled to refuse to answer a question on the ground that the answer might tend to incriminate him or her"
          ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is to refuse "on the ground that the answer might tend to incriminate"; where it would not, the subsection says nothing

-- src:22238 | (8) An inspector may cause notes of any examination under this
-- src:22239 | Part to be recorded and reduced to writing and to be read to or by and
-- src:22240 | signed by the person examined and any such signed notes may except
-- src:22241 | in the case of any answer which that person would not have been
-- src:22242 | required to give but for subsection (6) thereafter be used in evidence
-- src:22243 | in any legal proceedings against that person.
@ref s 236(8) (src:22238-22243)
GIVEN `the examination is an examination under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(8) the inspector may cause notes of the examination to be recorded, reduced to writing and read to or by and signed by the person examined` MEANS
    IF `the examination is an examination under Part 9`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "any examination under this Part"

@ref s 236(8) (src:22238-22243)
GIVEN `the notes were recorded, reduced to writing, read to or by the person and signed by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer is one the person would not have been required to give but for subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(8) the signed notes may be used in evidence in legal proceedings against the person` MEANS
    IF `the answer is one the person would not have been required to give but for subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any such signed notes may except in the case of any answer which that person would not have been required to give but for subsection (6) thereafter be used in evidence"; an "except" met
    ELSE (IF `the notes were recorded, reduced to writing, read to or by the person and signed by the person`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "such signed notes"; unsigned notes are outside it
